        "id": 6460
      },
      "writtenOn": "2014-06-08T16:16:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So you confirm unlimited trusts do not get locked by confirming sql_model.lock is none, correct?  Just curiously why is the self.assertIsNotNone(lock_id)  also needed?",
      "revId": "73f916900bc13d72f9184a6ec9cf5125ad3df874",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1ae5cdf2_9d5ae84e",
        "filename": "keystone/tests/test_backend_sql.py",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 401,
      "author": {
        "id": 2903
      },
      "writtenOn": "2014-06-09T16:39:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The isNotNone assert shows that we have a lock_id, the context manager yields (passes the information back in the with statement) the lock_id. \n\nIt\u0027s the responsibility of the external service to know if they hold the lock in a race condition.  The context manager should prevent it from racing, but be safe.",
      "parentUuid": "1ae5cdf2_8087fd11",
      "revId": "73f916900bc13d72f9184a6ec9cf5125ad3df874",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
